        "#7 Three findings\n",
        "\n",
        "Finding 1: Risk comes in waves. The volatility chart in section 5 spikes during the same crash periods from section 3, then goes quiet again. A model that assumes risk is always the same would completely miss this.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finding 2: Extreme days happen more than a normal bell curve expects. The number from section 4 shows that both big up days and big down days happen more often than \"normal\" predicts. That's why my simulation uses real historical days instead of made up ones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finding 3: Some of the market's big gain is just inflation. Section 6 shows that once you account for inflation, the real growth is smaller than the number people usually quote. Going up 5 times isn't the same as being 5 times richer."
