      "source": [
        "#8 Monte Carlo: simulating one year forward\n",
        "If I put a lump sum into the S&P 500 today (meaning the last price in my data), what's a realistic guess at what it looks like one year later? I don't just want \"it averages 7 to 8% a year,\" I want the full range of what could actually happen, since no single year is really \"average\" (sections 4 and 5 show that).\n",
        "\n",
        "How I'm doing it, step by step:\n",
        "\n",
        "The thing I don't know is the daily return (section 4).\n",
        "I turn that into a random guess two different ways: one where I randomly pull real days from my actual data (with repeats allowed), and one where I just generate fake numbers from a normal bell curve using the same average and spread.\n",
        "I repeat that for 252 days in a row (roughly one trading year), then do the whole thing over again 10,000 times.\n",
        "Then I look at all 10,000 possible year end prices, mark where the low, middle, and high ranges land, and turn it into a probability instead of one single number."
      ],
      "id": "h0LUp_K2YmRF"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "RFXb6gJSYmRF",
        "outputId": "84be3e12-8859-4c55-b8fd-8790e2147bfb"
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Simulating forward from the last real close: $6,896.24 on 2025-12-30\n",
            "10,000 simulated years complete for both methods.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(5641)\n",
        "N_SIMS = 10_000\n",
        "HORIZON_DAYS = 252\n",
        "\n",
        "last_price = close.iloc[-1]\n",
        "last_date = close.index[-1].date()\n",
        "ret_pool = log_ret.values\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Simulating forward from the last real close: ${last_price:,.2f} on {last_date}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "end_price_bootstrap = np.empty(N_SIMS)\n",
        "for sim in range(N_SIMS):\n",
        "    path_returns = rng.choice(ret_pool, size=HORIZON_DAYS, replace=True)\n",
        "    end_price_bootstrap[sim] = last_price * np.exp(path_returns.sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "end_price_normal = np.empty(N_SIMS)\n",
        "for sim in range(N_SIMS):\n",
        "    path_returns = rng.normal(daily_mu, daily_sd, size=HORIZON_DAYS)\n",
        "    end_price_normal[sim] = last_price * np.exp(path_returns.sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"10,000 simulated years complete for both methods.\")"
      ],
